        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> But it doesn't seem to recognize them and surrounds both sides with whichever bracket I use first:\n> \n> -- I select abc\n> abc\n> -- I do gsa to add a surrounding pair and type 「\n> 「abc「\n> -- I don't get 「abc」\n> \n> Maybe it has something to do with these brackets being unicode and not being one byte.\n\nWhat you describe is the functionality of 'mini.surround', not 'mini.pairs' (with `gsa` coming from LazyVim, I presume). The 'mini.pairs' use case would be pressing `「` in Insert mode and the whole pair `「」` appears with cursor between brackets. The provided config seems to be good for it.\n\nHere is the 'mini.surround' setup for one such bracket (similarly expand further for others):\n\n```lua\nrequire('mini.surround').setup({\n  custom_surroundings = {\n    ['「'] = { input = { '「().-()」' }, output = { left = '「', right = '」' } },\n  },\n})\n```",
